{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1579515193,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDM0MDQ2NDg5Mw=="},"target":"073bc0a3806ec3e5ab60c7b088496b6628d10f6ac447c6498f08e966fb7a5871","message":"As witnessed in a bunch of contexts now (e.g. #4054 #4026) we are susceptible to failure due to windows short paths (these beauties: `C:\\SHORT~1`). We use lexical operations and comparisons on paths in many places, and we always assume full/long paths. Hence this is a big deal on windows. In particular the GitHub CI machines are set up in a way that make them appear frequently.\n\nAs seen here https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/4054#issuecomment-576150443 switching from `op.realpath` to `Path.resolve()` takes care of this issue in a convenient fashion. Therefore I propose to replace any use of `op.realpath` with the pathlib equivalent. This will not make any such issue go away, but it should substantially reduce our attack surface.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1579516061,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDM0MDQ3MzgyNg=="},"target":"073bc0a3806ec3e5ab60c7b088496b6628d10f6ac447c6498f08e966fb7a5871","message":"As witnessed in a bunch of contexts now (e.g. #4054 #4026) we are susceptible to failure due to windows short paths (these beauties: `C:\\SHORT~1`). We use lexical operations and comparisons on paths in many places, and we always assume full/long paths. Hence this is a big deal on windows. In particular the GitHub CI machines are set up in a way that make them appear frequently.\n\nAs seen here https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/4054#issuecomment-576150443 switching from `op.realpath` to `Path.resolve()` takes care of this issue in a convenient fashion. Therefore I propose to replace any use of `op.realpath` with the pathlib equivalent. This will not make any such issue go away, but it should substantially reduce our attack surface.\n\nThere is a complication: `resolve(strict=False)` was only introduced with PY3.6, before that it required a path to exist in order to be able to call this method.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1579515130,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI5NjIzNDQ2NTg="},"added":["windows"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1579515130,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI5NjIzNDQ2NjE="},"added":["severity-important"],"removed":[]}]}